        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Political Reformers - Overview",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "The distinction matters for counterfactual analysis. Reformers work with what exists; revolutionaries burn it down and build. Both can produce durable change; neither guarantees it. Revolutions have a documented failure mode: they destroy existing institutions without building replacement ones and reliably produce authoritarian consolidation (Robespierre → Napoleon; Lenin → Stalin; Mao's Cultural Revolution; Castro's permanent emergency)."
    }
